  id: Transverse_pectoral_muscle_Superficial_pectoral
  partName: Transverse_pectoral_muscle_Superficial_pectoral
  descriptionChunks:
  - 'The transverse pectoral muscle runs across the chest and functions to adduct
    the forelimbs, drawing them toward the midline of the body. It plays an important
    role in stabilizing the chest and maintaining proper posture during movement. '
  - By controlling limb positioning, it contributes to coordinated locomotion and
    prevents excessive lateral movement. This muscle works in synergy with other
    chest muscles to provide both stability and controlled force, ensuring efficient
    and balanced motion.
